{% macro stack_input(cap=false) %}{{ "The" if cap else "the" }} stack — branch and commit per assembled PR, bottom first; empty before the first assembly{% endmacro %}
{% macro open_pr_rule(followup=false) %}Nothing is inserted at or before the open PR. A delta may grow it, shrink it or re-split it into itself plus new entries after it, remove it only when the delta's triggering document is an **Empty round** triage, and restates its `size`; its branch is renamed only when an assembly escalation says the name exists{% if followup %}, and never when the entry is inherited: its name existing is the point, and the assembler moves it (**Inherited-entry rule**){% endif %}.{% endmacro %}
{% macro recreated_assembled_rule() %}A re-scope never empties an assembled entry: a PR whose commit would become empty is removed through a re-created follow-up, not by fixup.{% endmacro %}
{% macro recreated_tail_rule() %}In a re-created stack an inherited entry not yet re-created is in the free tail: it may be removed or re-scoped, never renamed. An inherited entry a delta removes, from the free tail or as the open entry after an **Empty round**, is listed as `removed:` with the reason.{% endmacro %}
